{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Acknowledge untracked broker position #{{ vm.discrepancy_id }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<section class="reconcile-orphan-acknowledge" data-orphan-acknowledge="true">
  <h1>Untracked broker position #{{ vm.discrepancy_id }}</h1>

  <section class="pre-resolution-context" data-pre-context="true">
    <dl class="context-pairs">
      <dt>Ticker</dt><dd>{{ vm.ticker }}</dd>
      <dt>Detail</dt><dd>{{ vm.delta_text }}</dd>
      <dt>Created at</dt><dd>{{ vm.created_at }}</dd>
      <dt>Reconciliation run</dt><dd>#{{ vm.run_id }}</dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="muted">
      The broker holds this position but the journal has no matching open
      trade. Journal the position (so the ledger-derived equity matches the
      broker NLV), then acknowledge here to clear this finding.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">CLI parity: <code>swing journal discrepancy resolve
      {{ vm.discrepancy_id }} --resolution acknowledged_immaterial</code></p>
  </section>

  {#- Arc 20-C (D23): surface the DURABLE path ABOVE the one-shot acknowledge.
      A recurring broker holding (e.g. a long-term IPO buy-and-hold like RKLB)
      re-emits this finding every run until it is declared out-of-framework.
      V1 is GUIDANCE ONLY -- a web write to user-config.toml would be a new
      config-write surface (out of scope). #}
  <section class="oof-guidance" data-oof-guidance="true">
    <h2>Recurring holding? Declare it out-of-framework</h2>
    <p>
      If <strong>{{ vm.ticker }}</strong> is a position you hold OUTSIDE the
      swing framework (e.g. a long-term buy-and-hold), acknowledging it here
      clears the finding for THIS run only &mdash; it re-emits every
      reconciliation run. The durable fix is to declare the ticker
      out-of-framework so the orphan pass stops flagging it.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Add the ticker to
        <code>~/swing-data/user-config.toml</code> (NOT the tracked
        <code>swing.config.toml</code>):
<pre class="config-stanza">[reconciliation]
out_of_framework_tickers = ["{{ vm.ticker }}"]</pre>
        (append <code>{{ vm.ticker }}</code> to the list if the section already
        exists).
      </li>
      <li>
        Clear the existing orphan row(s) for the declared set:
        <code>swing schwab resolve-out-of-framework</code>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted">
      <strong>Which path?</strong>
      Choose <em>declare out-of-framework</em> for a position you will keep
      holding at the broker but never manage as a swing trade (stops the
      recurring finding permanently).
      Choose <em>journal the position</em> (open a trade for it) if it IS a
      swing position the journal is simply missing.
      Choose the <em>one-shot acknowledge</em> below only for a genuinely
      one-off finding you do not expect to see again.
    </p>
  </section>

  {% if vm.error_band_message %}
  <section class="error-band">
    <p>{{ vm.error_band_message }}</p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <form
    method="post"
    action="{{ vm.form_action }}"
    hx-post="{{ vm.form_action }}"
    hx-headers='{"HX-Request": "true"}'
    hx-target="body"
    data-orphan-acknowledge-form="true">

    <fieldset>
      <legend>Acknowledge (optional reason)</legend>
      <textarea name="resolution_reason" rows="3"
        placeholder="e.g. Journaled the IPO shares; untracked holding known."
        >{{ vm.prior_resolution_reason }}</textarea>
      <p class="muted">
        Clears the finding to <code>acknowledged_immaterial</code>. A reason is
        optional for this resolution.
      </p>
    </fieldset>

    <button type="submit" class="primary">Acknowledge and clear</button>
  </form>
</section>
{% endblock %}
